      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is there for developers to override any of the members. This series of patches makes all of the new_type_ref() functions take kwargs to reduce the need for creating refs manually.\n\nInstead of:\n\n    ref \u003d dict(a\u003d1, b\u003d2)\n\nThe dev can call:\n\n    ref \u003d new_type_ref(a\u003d1, b\u003d2)\n\nUsing kwargs makes the code resilient to changes in the models. We can always police the inputs if and when needed.",
